a1                       Welcome to META-Usenet!
                       -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-

  This is a UseNet->CNet shell that I (Heavy Metal) wrote for CNet Amiga.
  It acts exactly like CNet Amiga in many areas and similar in others.
  If you can use CNet Amiga, you can use Meta-UseNet.  It's easy.
  
                              Beginner tips:
    ====================================================================
       After you have chosen your netname and get to the MetaUseNet
       Main prompt,  you can do the following to get a quick start:

     1) Enter "JA" to join all newsgroups and then use "L" to list them.
     2) enter a newsgroup number to enter that newsgroup/subboard.
     3) enter "S" to scan the messages (news).
     4) enter R<number> to read a message, where <number> is the number
        listed to the left of the message.
     5) enter "?" at most prompts for help/menu.
    ====================================================================

Reading and replying to UseNet messages costs you NIL/NOTHING/NADA so enjoy!
